=======================
Build/Run Instructions:
=======================

    make clean && make build

This will produce a top level executable named "412alloc"


======
Usage:
======

    ./412alloc -h
    ./412alloc -x <iloc file>
    ./412alloc k <iloc file>    # 3 <= k <= 64



===============================
Command Line Options Explained:
===============================

    -h
        Prints a help/usage message and exits.
    -x
        Scans, parses, and renames <file>. Prints the renamed IR to stdout.
    k <file>
        Allocate with k physical registers (3 <= k <= 64) on <file> and prints the allocated ILOC to stdout.



================
Flags Explained:
================

If multiple flags are provided, they are prioritized in order of -h, then -x, else k.
if no flag/k is given, the file cannot be opened, or k is outside the allowed range, the program terminates and reports the error.


    

